-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 21 16:43:11 UTC 2026 - Benoît Monin <benoit.monin@gmx.fr>

- update to version 13.1.2:
  * FIX: MagicLink: Fix issue were new URL parser can consume
    Python Markdown placeholders unexpectedly (#3062).
- additional changes from version 13.1.1:
  * FIX: PathConverter, B64: Treat links with a scheme but
    no network location, such as magnet:?xt=..., sms:+123, or
    xmpp:user@example.org, as URLs instead of relative paths.
  * FIX: StripHTML: Match HTML tag and attribute names case
    insensitively so that attributes such as ONCLICK are stripped
    just like onclick.
  * FIX: StripHTML: Improve scanning time caused by
    unclosed comments, script, or style tags and long runs of
    whitespace. Output is unchanged.
  * FIX: B64 and PathConverter: Match HTML tag and attribute
    names case insensitively (<IMG SRC="...">), and do not treat
    a tag that merely starts with script or style (<scripty>)
    as a script or style tag.
  * FIX: Keys: Fix quoted keys dropping escaped backslashes
    that come before another escape.
  * FIX: Keys: Fix a + inside a quoted key being treated as a
    key separator instead of content.
  * FIX: B64: Improve scanning time caused by unclosed script,
    style, or comment tags and long runs of whitespace. Unclosed
    script, style, and comment tags are now treated as running
    to the end of the content, as browsers do, so images after
    them are no longer converted.
  * FIX: PathConverter: Improve scanning time caused by
    unclosed script, style, or comment tags and long runs of
    whitespace. Unclosed script, style, and comment tags are now
    treated as running to the end of the content, as browsers do,
    so links after them are no longer converted.
  * FIX: PathConverter: Fix src (and href) on script and style
    tags not being converted when the tag is listed in tags. Only
    the content of these tags is now skipped.
  * FIX: PathConverter and B64: Do not convert text that
    merely looks like a src or href attribute inside the value
    of another attribute.
  * FIX: BetterEm: Fix quadratic processing time in emphasis
    handling for many unclosed openers which the rule of 3 keeps
    an ambiguous closer from pairing with, such as *a **b repeated.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Nov 12 21:09:38 UTC 2026 - Benoît Monin <benoit.monin@gmx.fr>

- update to version 13.1:
  * NEW: Snippets: Respect the Retry-After header when a URL
    responds with a 429. The server's requested delay is used
    instead of our backoff, and the snippet fails right away
    if it is longer than the longest we would wait ourselves
    (backoff_factor times max_retries).
  * NEW: Snippets: Split snippet processing into steps
    that an extension can override (parse_snippet_target,
    select_snippet_lines, and process_snippet_lines) to add
    notation or change included content, and add get_syntax_mask
    to find which lines are snippet notation so they can be left
    alone. (#3040)
  * FIX: Fix an issue where only our test environment required
    Python Markdown 3.10.3. Installs must require this.
  * FIX: Snippets: Fix quadratic time complexity when parsing
    very long runs of ; or - in content, and very long snippet
    paths with line ranges.
  * FIX: Quotes, Details (legacy), Tabbed (legacy), FancyLists,
    Blocks, and Snippets: Gracefully stop short of the recursion
    limit when content is nested too deeply, instead of raising
    a RecursionError. This includes content nested inside of a
    document structure that is already deep, such as a quote or
    tab inside of many nested lists. Content past the limit is
    no longer specially processed (Snippets skips includes past
    the limit, as it does for cyclic includes).
- additional changes from version 13.0:
  * BREAK: Arithmatex: Generic mode is now the default mode
    as the old MathJax script approach has not been supported in
    MathJax for a long time now. We still provide script approach
    and have updated configuration to get it properly working in
    recent MathJax versions.
  * BREAK: Arithmatex: Non-generic mode now escapes content in
    script to prevent closing </script> from causing unintended
    behavior. Guidance on configuration for non-generic mode has
    been updated in the documentation.
  * NEW: Require at least Python Markdown 3.10.3 for performance
    improvements.
  * NEW: Drop Python 3.10 and require Python >= 3.11.5 as
    possessive quantifiers are broken on lower versions.
  * NEW: MagicLink: Bare http://, https://, and www. links now
    follow GFM's extended autolink rules for what is considered
    the end of a link (trailing punctuation, entities, unbalanced
    ) and ]) and what a link can follow. Links no longer start
    after arbitrary punctuation (quotes are still allowed),
    and http://host style links with a short host are allowed.
    * FIX: Critic: Fix quadratic (and cubic for substitutions)
    time complexity when parsing a large number of unclosed
    CriticMarkup openers by replacing the regular expression with
    a linear time scanner.
  * FIX: PathConverter, B64: Handle elements with unquoted
    attributes.
  * FIX: Arithmatex: Fix generic mode output when tex_inline_wrap
    or tex_block_wrap contain braces.
  * FIX: InlineHilite: Fix regression related to unmatched
    opening and closing.
  * FIX: FancyLists: Keep i and I in alphabetical lists after
    a blank line.
  * FIX: BracketSpan: Fix unwanted colon attributes with
    {:...} syntax.
  * FIX: Snippets: Fix escaped section markers starting or
    ending a section before its start.
  * FIX: StripHTML: Fix crash when strip_comments is disabled.
  * FIX: Quotes: Fix callouts in indented blockquotes.
  * FIX: Details, Admonitions, SaneHeaders: Improve performance
    of header patterns.
  * FIX: Blocks.HTML: Improve performance of HTML patterns.
  * FIX: MagicLink: Fix URLs with balanced parentheses or
    brackets losing their closing character.
  * FIX: MagicLink: Improve performance of link and email
    patterns by removing excessive backtracking.
  * FIX: ProgressBar: Fix crash on malformed 100 percent values
    like [=100,0%].
  * FIX: BracketSpan: Fix text being dropped or misplaced when
    an unpaired [ precedes a span that is returned from the cache,
    e.g. [[]{#a}[b[]{#c}.
  * FIX: BetterEm, Tilde, Caret, Mark: Apply the CommonMark
    "rule of 3" so an ambiguous closing delimiter can skip
    an incompatible opener and pair with an earlier one,
    e.g. __[A](u){target="_blank"}__: x.
  * FIX: BetterEm, Tilde, Caret, Mark: Better handling of
    Python Markdown placeholders when when evaluating CommonMark
    punctuation rules.
  * FIX: Blocks.Caption: Fix crash when a numbered caption is
    nested inside a figure not created by the caption block.
  * FIX: BetterEm, Tilde, Caret, Mark: Fix text being dropped
    when a stray delimiter that cannot open or close appears
    between delimiter pairs parsed together, e.g. ***l* * **e**.
  * FIX: BetterEm, Tilde, Caret, Mark: Fix text being dropped
    or misplaced when unused delimiters inside a parsed span
    were reprocessed against delimiter pairs found later in the
    same text.
  * FIX: Tilde, Caret: Fix a crash when a subscript or superscript
    with no space allowed starts inside emphasis, e.g. *a ~b~*
    with delete disabled.
  * FIX: BetterEm, Tilde, Caret, Mark: Unusable delimiters
    dropped by another delimiter's region no longer leave stale
    space tracking that can reject valid pairs later.
  * FIX: Blocks.Caption: Fix crash when a numbered caption is
    nested inside a figure not created by the caption block.
- increase minimum python version to 3.11.5
- increase minimum Markdown version to 3.10.3

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 20 17:59:26 UTC 2026 - Benoît Monin <benoit.monin@gmx.fr>

